WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.370
I asked our school agent to book

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.730
the bus for the science trip.

3
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.360
It said it couldn’t.

4
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.590
I was annoyed at first.

5
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.190
Then I realised: it had no

6
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.110
tool for booking!

7
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.730
Today: what an agent’s tools allow, and

8
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.830
what a good agent does when they don’t.

9
00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.170
Before it acts, the model reads

10
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.250
your request and the list of

11
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.630
tools that are switched on.

12
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.930
Darsi Tiny has ten, from a

13
00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.410
calculator to reminders and messages.

14
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.410
It acts only through those tools,

15
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.270
so no tool means no job.

16
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.410
Each tool needs details.

17
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.110
The weather tool needs a place and a day.

18
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.130
The timetable needs a class and a day.

19
00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.630
The model copies those details

20
00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.450
from your words into the call.

21
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.070
So a request can go four ways.

22
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.960
It uses a tool.

23
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.650
It says the tool it needs is off.

24
00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:02.370
It says it can’t, because no tool fits.

25
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.130
Or it asks for a missing detail.

26
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.590
I switched the weather tool off and

27
00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.810
asked about Kafi: it said the tool is

28
00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.530
off, instead of guessing.

29
00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:17.150
Then I asked it to book a bus ticket.

30
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.140
No tool can, so it said so.

31
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.820
What if you leave out a detail?

32
00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.700
Ask what the weather is tomorrow, and

33
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.400
Darsi Tiny asks back: which village?

34
00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:32.490
Reply Dala, and it calls the weather tool.

35
00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.480
Asking beats guessing.

36
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:36.370
Quick check!

37
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.840
The reminder tool is switched off,

38
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.080
and you ask for a reminder.

39
00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.880
What should a good agent do?

40
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.720
Say the tool is off.

41
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.060
An agent that pretends hides

42
00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.100
what really happened.

43
00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.220
Being told no is useful: you

44
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.100
know to do it yourself.

45
00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.620
But it doesn’t always know its limits.

46
00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.140
Ask what class 9Z has tomorrow, a

47
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.120
class that doesn’t exist, and it

48
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.120
calls the timetable for 9C.

49
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.030
Ask what is the capital of France,

50
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:12.910
and it tries the glossary.

51
00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.120
So check every call.

52
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.240
In the app, ask about the weather

53
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.740
in Kafi, then switch the weather

54
00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.520
tool off and ask again.

55
00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.050
Ask for something no tool can

56
00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.870
do, and leave out a detail.

57
00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.240
Then try class 9Z, and read

58
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.340
the check under the call.

59
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.080
Your turn.

60
00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:37.010
I asked what the weather is tomorrow, and

61
00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.010
the agent asked me: which village?

62
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:40.320
Why?

63
00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.730
It needs a place.

64
00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.450
Remember: an agent acts only through

65
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.950
the tools that are on, and fills in

66
00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.290
details from your words.

67
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.720
A good agent says when it can’t, or

68
00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.140
asks, instead of guessing.

69
00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.760
Try it in class tomorrow:

70
00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.180
play The toolbox.

71
00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.360
Groups get six tool cards, and

72
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.180
you read out requests.

73
00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:07.150
For each, they decide: use a tool, ask

74
00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.530
for a detail, or say I can’t.

75
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.420
Then turn a card over and play again.
